A. $\alpha$-Glucose and $\alpha$-Galactose differ only in configuration at $\text{C}-4$ $\to$ Epimers (IV);
B. $\alpha$-Glucose and $\beta$-Glucose differ at the anomeric $\text{C}-1$ carbon $\to$ Anomers (III);
C. Glucose (aldohexose) and Fructose (ketohexose) have the same formula $\text{C}_6\text{H}_{12}\text{O}_6$ $\to$ Functional isomers (I);
D. Glucose ($\text{C}_6\text{H}_{12}\text{O}_6$) and Ribose ($\text{C}_5\text{H}_{10}\text{O}_5$) differ by a $-\text{CHOH}-$ unit $\to$ Homologues (II).
